Summary report - Getting started with Digital VLSI SOC Design and Planning
RISC-V SoC Design: RTL to Tapeout – Quick Overview
Target Chips: 100–130 MHz programmable chips, similar to those used in Arduino boards.
Core Concept: RISC-V architecture enables open-source, customizable SoC development.
Microcontroller vs Microprocessor:
Microcontroller: Integrated CPU + memory + peripherals; ideal for embedded systems.
Microprocessor: CPU only; relies on external components for full system functionality.

Design Flow Summary
Specification Definition - Based on application needs, written in C or system-level language.
RTL Design - Hardware described using Verilog at Register Transfer Level (RTL).
Synthesis - RTL converted to Gate-Level Netlist using tools like Yosys.
IP Integration - Combine processor core, peripherals, analog IPs, and macros.
Tapeout Preparation - Final layout and verification for ASIC fabrication.

